Experiments for "Formalizing the Connectivity Theorem for the Matrix
Multiplication Flip Graph in ACL2" (ACL2 Workshop 2026)

Supporting material for the paper's section on working with a language model.
Nothing here is part of the proof in the parent directory.

Certification
-------------

  cert.pl -j 4 unassisted/top.lisp cross-check/xcheck-defs.lisp

certifies all 34 books, in about half an hour.

Running the cross-check
-----------------------

With the books above certified, from cross-check/:

  ACL2_SYSTEM_BOOKS=<books> <acl2> < xcheck-tests.lsp > xcheck-tests.out

runs the sixteen properties with ACL2s cgen at 300 trials each;
xcheck-tests.out is our transcript of that run.  Fifteen properties hold;
prop-b-naive is false on purpose and records the flip convention difference
the paper reports.

  python3 rename.py

regenerates the renamed books of cross-check/ from unassisted/.

Subfolders
----------

unassisted/     the 24 books produced by the unassisted experiment, as that
                session produced them, with the README.md it wrote
cross-check/    the ACL2s cross-check of our connectivity theorem against
                theirs: the renamed books, xcheck-defs.lisp with the
                translation and the properties, and xcheck-tests.lsp
